{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"8788a0f20de19bad","type":"group","x":-288,"y":-180,"width":1236,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"220b620ad13339a2","type":"text","text":"**[Investigation]**\nYou know the number of segments and DC for a lock or trap you are attempting to pick. If unlocking it would trigger a trap, you identify that before rolling.\n\nAdditionally, you can always tell if multiple Clues were left by the same person.","x":-268,"y":1940,"width":348,"height":257},
		{"id":"aa5bd4b922e80145","type":"text","text":"**[Well-Informed]**\nWhen interacting with a character for the first time, you can request 1 special insight about their faction, location, or recent activity; you can begin a Project to request more special insights about the same character. ","x":160,"y":1962,"width":348,"height":213},
		{"id":"b59fa9e0223289a0","type":"text","text":"**[Vigilance]**\nIf rolling to Guard the group in a hostile tile, roll with Advantage (1). \n\nYou can rest while wearing up to Bulk (4) of armor without penalty.","x":-268,"y":1671,"width":348,"height":178},
		{"id":"3998484b392510f5","type":"text","text":"**[Mimicry]**\nWhen disguised as another, pick two aspects: appearance, conduct, persona. Your chosen aspects will never arouse suspicion.\n\nAfter performing the *Disguise* rest action, the next Clue you leave leads back to a character of your choice.","x":160,"y":1300,"width":348,"height":260},
		{"id":"86a5bbeba48b24f4","type":"text","text":"**[Disguise]**\nYou gain the *Disguise* rest action. It reads as follows:\n*Disguise* allows you to create a disguise that allows you to visually masquerade as a member of any faction.","x":-268,"y":1330,"width":348,"height":198},
		{"id":"22df1c6f68843d97","type":"text","text":"**[Smuggling]**\nYou can prevent an item of Bulk (1) or less from being seen, found, or taken against your will so long as it remains on your person. Additionally, you can Pickpocket an amount of Bulk (0) items equal to both your Finesse and Cunning.","x":160,"y":1040,"width":348,"height":224},
		{"id":"34fb863380506f17","type":"text","text":"**[Sleight of Hand]**\nIf rolling a Contest to Pickpocket a target who is unaware of your presence, roll with Advantage (1).","x":-268,"y":1091,"width":348,"height":123},
		{"id":"50eda4efac4f56f5","type":"text","text":"**[Camouflage]**\nIf rolling for Stealth, you gain Advantage (1), even if you are within line of sight, so long as you remain motionless. Activating a Contraption does not reveal your location.","x":160,"y":800,"width":348,"height":187},
		{"id":"25f73dd2b1c2c680","type":"text","text":"**[Stealth]**\nIf rolling for Stealth outside a target's line of sight, roll with Advantage (1). ","x":-268,"y":848,"width":348,"height":91},
		{"id":"1bb4832b47b29d4a","type":"text","text":"**[Forensics]**\nYou can always identify the source of a character's damage and for how long someone has been dead. You also gain the *Theorize* rest action. It reads as follows:\n\n*Theorize* allows you to identify all relevant details of a skirmish which occurred on your current tile, including what parties were involved and how they exited the scene.","x":580,"y":1902,"width":348,"height":334},
		{"id":"6e5196bd9bb2013e","type":"text","text":"**[Botany]**\nYou can find a Trace Resource Node that yields fiber when Surveying on any tile where flora could reasonably be found. The Resource Node disappears when you exit the tile.","x":-268,"y":580,"width":348,"height":187},
		{"id":"607c967ae34e7802","type":"text","text":"**[Forage]**\nWhile Gathering for fibers or alchemical resources, you harvest twice the normal amount. You are always aware if a plant, Potion, or Ration is dangerous to consume.","x":160,"y":580,"width":348,"height":187},
		{"id":"45355bf7bf93f528","type":"text","text":"**[Alchemist]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Alchemy' Skill requirement. Your [Botany] Resource Nodes can yield basic alchemical resources instead.","x":580,"y":596,"width":348,"height":155},
		{"id":"e7b9d145940aaf8f","type":"text","text":"**[Tracking]**\nYou can find a Trace Resource Node that yields carcasses when Surveying on any tile where wildlife could reasonably be found. The Resource Node disappears when you exit the tile.","x":-268,"y":324,"width":348,"height":188},
		{"id":"a506b2868b21feed","type":"text","text":"**[Astronomy]**\nYou can never become nonmagically lost so long as you have clear view of the night sky, and the range of your sight on moonless and moonlit nights increases by Blinded (5). Additionally, you reduce Travel for your entire group by 1 segment on unpaved tiles.","x":580,"y":298,"width":348,"height":239},
		{"id":"27e10a1958ef7361","type":"text","text":"**[Navigation]**\nWhen Scouting a tile you learn of 1 additional landmark and modifier affecting that tile. The size of your [Tracking] Resource Nodes increases to Moderate.","x":160,"y":324,"width":348,"height":188},
		{"id":"b73af3f45c235f7c","type":"text","text":"**[Conceal Presence]**\nYou leave 1 less Clue, to a minimum of 1. You gain the *Conceal presence* rest action. It reads as follows:\n\n*Conceal presence* allows you to hide yourself and up to Bulk (20) of items on a tile. Unless a character is told where this cache is, they cannot discover it through nonmagical means, and cannot find you until you take an Explore or Travel action.","x":580,"y":895,"width":348,"height":319},
		{"id":"688b3340df29be15","type":"text","text":"**[Beast Tamer]**\nChoose one non-human Kin type. You create a familiar Hireling, who cannot be demoralized and provides a unique bonus to either Projects, Journeys, or Challenge Clocks based on its Kinship and determined by the GM.","x":580,"y":11,"width":348,"height":213},
		{"id":"53c061ddfc5bc67d","type":"text","text":"**[Animal Handling]**\nYou can have 1 additional Hireling beyond your max, so long as it is an animal. Additionally, you can identify an animal by its appearance, tracks or remains; in doing so you can identify its Kin type.","x":-268,"y":19,"width":348,"height":198},
		{"id":"efe7d2a536ece3fa","type":"text","text":"**[Appraisal]**\nYou can learn an item's approximate region, culture, or time period of origin when observing it for the first time.","x":-284,"y":6519,"width":348,"height":157},
		{"id":"8d6f4c6b0db195f6","type":"text","text":"**[Literacy]**\nYou are literate and can read languages that you know how to speak.","x":-284,"y":6760,"width":348,"height":120},
		{"id":"675036460a99820b","type":"text","text":"**[Language]**\nYou can speak an additional language beyond Common (Low Marathan) and your native tongue. You can take this skill multiple times, picking a new language each time.","x":-284,"y":6920,"width":348,"height":180},
		{"id":"4418a495a2a23929","type":"text","text":"**[Lore]**\nWhen choosing this skill, select an appropriate niche topic of study. Anytime this niche topic of study would be applicable, and no other bonuses would apply, you may apply a +5 bonus instead of the usual +1. You may take this skill multiple times, picking a new topic of study each time.\n\n**[Topics of Study]**\n- Dialects\n- Religion*\n- Occultism\n- High Society\n- Mathematics\n- Cryptography\n- Legal System\n- Codicology\n- Heresiology*\n- Tidal Studies\n- Optical Theory\n- Painting\n- Calligraphy\n- Music Theory\n- Farming Techniques\n- Animal Ecology\n- Regional History*\n- Military Strategy\n- Farming Techniques","x":-284,"y":7140,"width":1224,"height":740},
		{"id":"1deb4c10d6094543","type":"text","text":"**[Dancing]**\nYou gain the *Shake a leg* rest action. It reads as follows:\n*Shake a leg* allows you to rally a group and increase morale. Anyone not taking a rest action gains an Inspiration, which is wasted if not used by the next rest. If another character takes the *Work a crowd* rest action, the bonus is increased to 2 Inspiration.","x":-284,"y":5480,"width":348,"height":290},
		{"id":"a108663a65338989","type":"text","text":"**[Husbandry]**\nYour animal Hirelings require 1 less ration to maintain, to a minimum of 1 per Hireling, and roll all Morale Saves with Advantage (1).\n\n","x":160,"y":40,"width":348,"height":155},
		{"id":"443f3c57e3c6b5b1","type":"text","text":"<div class=\"centered\">\n\n## EXP Cost / Bonus: 1 / +1\n\n</div>","x":-268,"y":-160,"width":348,"height":100},
		{"id":"d32cd5fde5bd54b2","type":"text","text":"<div class=\"centered\">\n\n## EXP Cost / Bonus: 3 / +2\n\n</div>","x":160,"y":-160,"width":348,"height":100},
		{"id":"02211036606eec55","type":"text","text":"<div class=\"centered\">\n\n## EXP Cost / Bonus: 5 / +3\n\n</div>","x":580,"y":-160,"width":348,"height":100},
		{"id":"cac30bbf34714392","type":"text","text":"**[Fencing]**\nChoose one region you've done business in. You gain a fence there, a character who will buy or sell any item off the books for a reduced price; you can begin a Project to source a specific rare item or illegal good through your fence.","x":160,"y":6489,"width":348,"height":217},
		{"id":"eb0fcc79400edcc7","type":"text","text":"**[Oration]**\nYou can have 1 additional Hireling beyond your max, so long as it is a human. Additionally, you can identify a person's profession, social class, or origin by their speech and bearing; in doing so you can identify what faction or community they belong to.","x":-284,"y":6180,"width":348,"height":239},
		{"id":"bfcc921c1e19ea88","type":"text","text":"**[Authority]**\nChoose one faction or community which you are a part of. You can create a loyalist, which is a human Hireling from that group with a +1, +2, and +3 Skill determined by the GM. Your loyalist costs a further 25% less coin to utilize and cannot be demoralized.","x":580,"y":6180,"width":348,"height":239},
		{"id":"0e4b3afd56802f7e","type":"text","text":"**[Music]**\nYou gain the *Work a crowd* rest action. It reads as follows:\n*Work a crowd* allows you to sway a gathering and bolster spirits. Everyone who hears it can ignore the first Minor Wound they would gain while Journeying. If another character takes the *Shake a leg* rest action, everyone can ignore the first 2 Minor Wounds.","x":-284,"y":5840,"width":348,"height":290},
		{"id":"84f992049790c5d1","type":"text","text":"**[Hauling]**\nThe heaviest single unequipped item you are carrying takes up 3 less Encumbrance, to a minimum of Bulk (1).","x":580,"y":5280,"width":348,"height":123},
		{"id":"8ebee32ec5522a4c","type":"text","text":"**[Menial Labor]**\nYou provide a +1 Skill Bonus to all rolls made by other participants in a Project.","x":-284,"y":5296,"width":348,"height":91},
		{"id":"a0cf13aae03aef32","type":"text","text":"**[Masonry]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Masonry' Skill requirement.\n\nYou can treat stone and brick objects as if they were one Hardness lower, to a minimum of Hardness (1).","x":-284,"y":4998,"width":348,"height":206},
		{"id":"5055a2df582b23a1","type":"text","text":"**[Demolition]**\nYou ignore the DR of all objects. \n\nAdditionally, you reduce the segments for clearing Structures from a tile by 1. A Project can only have its total segments reduced to half by this Skill.","x":580,"y":4993,"width":348,"height":215},
		{"id":"0d9937f3544b2e7c","type":"text","text":"**[Acrobatics]**\nWhen you would take damage from Falling, make a Grace Save with the DC equal to the distance (in paces) fallen. On a success, take half damage. Additionally, when you perform the *Shake a leg* rest action, you gain +1 Speed until your next rest.","x":160,"y":5506,"width":348,"height":239},
		{"id":"ee515c1d04ddf1a2","type":"text","text":"**[Composing]**\nIf rolling to perform a song which you have composed, roll with Advantage (1). Additionally, when you perform the *Work a crowd* rest action, you gain +1 Max AP until your next rest.","x":160,"y":5892,"width":348,"height":187},
		{"id":"e8d000b38d86b117","type":"text","text":"**[Rhetoric]**\nYour human Hirelings require 25% less coin to utilize, and roll all Morale Saves with Advantage (1).","x":160,"y":6239,"width":348,"height":122},
		{"id":"94a4791cef14748a","type":"text","text":"**[Engineering]**\nObjects you create have their Hardness (#) increased by 1. \n\nYou reduce the segments for Intricate Structures you are building by 1.","x":580,"y":4740,"width":348,"height":178},
		{"id":"25d773970df2ca07","type":"text","text":"**[Carpentry]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Carpentry' Skill requirement. \n\nYou can treat wood objects as if they were one Hardness lower, to a minimum of Hardness (1).","x":-284,"y":4726,"width":348,"height":206},
		{"id":"94bf7fe4c935b5e9","type":"text","text":"**[Bowyer]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Bowyer' Skill requirement (Arrows, Bow and Crossbow Weapons).\n\nWhen you perform the *Equipment maintenance* rest action, you can reduce the Damaged (#) property on a wood weapon by 2, instead of 1.","x":160,"y":4520,"width":348,"height":256},
		{"id":"82051e0e9b015ede","type":"text","text":"**[Glassblower]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Glassblowing' Skill requirement (Alchemist's Tools, Glasswork, etc.).\n\nWhen you perform the *Drink a potion* rest action, you can scrape the bottom of the bottle for another character, applying the effects to both of you.","x":160,"y":4202,"width":348,"height":256},
		{"id":"b54dfea7921f2b07","type":"text","text":"**[Jeweler]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Jeweler' Skill requirement (Amulets, Rings, and Bracelets).\n\nYou can add Embellishments to any item, even if you didn't craft it. When adding Embellishments to items, you do so without any additional difficulty to its Challenge Clock.","x":580,"y":3920,"width":348,"height":282},
		{"id":"dfe32130b08b4553","type":"text","text":"**[Mining]**\nWhile Gathering working metals, iron, silver, and gold, you harvest twice the normal amount.\n\nYou can treat stone and brick objects as if they were 2 Hardness lower, to a minimum of Hardness (1). \n","x":160,"y":4985,"width":348,"height":231},
		{"id":"e5ddd0cb4fc398d8","type":"text","text":"**[Athletics]**\nThe first time in a day you would gain Fatigue outside of combat, you ignore it.","x":160,"y":5285,"width":348,"height":114},
		{"id":"53bde14d0fcf522e","type":"text","text":"**[Artistry]**\nYou can add Embellishments to items you craft. This allows you to add lore text, to give the item a colored name, and to add a quote to the bottom.","x":-268,"y":3983,"width":348,"height":155},
		{"id":"d06cc0a2978e3a3e","type":"text","text":"**[Jury-Rigging]**\nYou gain the *Produce trinket* rest action. It reads as follows:\n*Produce trinket* allows you to get a small, mundane object (a short length of rope, some nails, oil, small hammer, etc) for use on the next day. If not used by the next rest, the item is discarded.","x":-268,"y":2949,"width":348,"height":240},
		{"id":"1721b67423b9ea49","type":"text","text":"**[Weaponsmith]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Weaponsmith' Skill requirement (Metal Unarmed, Mass, Axe, Dagger, Sword, Spear, Hook, and Flail weapons).\n\nWhen you perform the *Equipment maintenance* rest action, you can reduce the Damaged (#) property on a metal weapon by 2, instead of 1.","x":580,"y":2923,"width":348,"height":293},
		{"id":"f9773733b7edbd4f","type":"text","text":"**[Seamster]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Needlework' Skill requirement (Robes, Sails and Banners).\n\nWhen you perform the *Equipment maintenance* rest action, you can convert an object or Equipment that requires fiber to craft into 3 times its Bulk (#) worth of Medicine (1).","x":160,"y":3587,"width":348,"height":282},
		{"id":"7ef80b3d4ee01e5f","type":"text","text":"**[Leatherworker]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Leatherwork' Skill requirement (Leather Armor, Tents, Travel Packs). \n\nWhen you perform the *Equipment maintenance* rest action, you can reduce the Damaged (#) property on non-metal armor by 2, instead of 1.","x":160,"y":3269,"width":348,"height":256},
		{"id":"106d222362fe47c1","type":"text","text":"**[Armorer]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Armorer' Skill requirement (Shield weapons and Metal Armor).\n\nWhen you perform the *Equipment maintenance* rest action, you can reduce the Damaged (#) property on metal armor by 2, instead of 1.","x":580,"y":3269,"width":348,"height":260},
		{"id":"413a8d9e2a7fea77","type":"text","text":"**[Blacksmith]**\nYou gain access to crafting recipes with the 'Blacksmith' Skill requirement. You also gain the *Equipment maintenance* rest action. It reads as follows:\n*Equipment maintenance* allows you to reduce the Damaged (#) property of one weapon or piece of armor by 1.","x":160,"y":2949,"width":348,"height":240},
		{"id":"e8a8186815869ffb","type":"text","text":"**[Cooking]**\nYou gain the *Cook a meal* rest action. It reads as follows:\n*Cook a meal* allows you to spend 1 additional ration per party member to cook them an invigorating meal. This raises their maximum AP by 2 until the next time they would gain Fatigue.","x":-268,"y":2640,"width":348,"height":239},
		{"id":"a6b37be2febb9abe","type":"text","text":"**[Culinarian]**\nWhen you perform the *Cook a meal* rest action, the party member gains 2 AP at initiative, increases their maximum AP by 1. If you have a Potion, you can include it in the meal to impart its effects to all participants.\n","x":580,"y":2653,"width":348,"height":213},
		{"id":"45dda9e9f5d2ad75","type":"text","text":"**[Butcher]**\nWhile Gathering carcasses, you harvest twice the normal amount. You can use carcasses in place of rations when resting or when you take the *Cook a meal* rest action.\n","x":160,"y":2666,"width":348,"height":187},
		{"id":"caee543fb1f898df","type":"text","text":"**[Surgery]**\nYou can assist in the recovery of a Major Wound as a Project. The patient adds your Surgery Skill bonus to the recovery Challenge Clock rolls. If they succeed, instead of turning the Major Wound into a scar, they clear it. If the Major Wound cannot be cleared (such as an amputation or an Equivalency) you can reduce recovery by 1 segment.","x":580,"y":2280,"width":348,"height":290},
		{"id":"0d038153fdea4292","type":"text","text":"**[First-Aid]**\nWhen you take the *Triage a wound* rest action, you can clear or disinfect an additional Wound.","x":-268,"y":2364,"width":348,"height":123}
	],
